## Original Content
Dans sa décision, le juge Paul Engelmayer a estimé que les arguments soulevés par la fille de Robert Maxwell, selon lesquels ses droits constitutionnels avaient été bafoués, étaient dénués de fondements sérieux.

## Summary
Judge Paul Engelmayer rejected Ghislaine Maxwell's request to annul her conviction, ruling that her claims of constitutional rights violations were unfounded. This decision in the Epstein case reaffirms the conviction.

## Key Points
- Judge Paul Engelmayer denied Ghislaine Maxwell's motion to overturn her conviction.
- Maxwell argued that her constitutional rights were violated, but the judge found these arguments baseless.
- The ruling pertains to the ongoing Epstein affair legal proceedings.


